[gd_scene load_steps=4 format=3 uid="uid://unitmeshinstance3dskinbyname"]

; The one variable: the binding by name. A MeshInstance3D sets `skin`, whose binds name the bones b0
; to b5 and carry no bone index, and the Skeleton3D has a root bone `extra` at index 0, so the
; bones b0 to b5 sit at indices 1 to 6. The ribbon bends along b0 to b5 as in
; unit-mesh-instance-3d-skinned-ribbon.tscn. Without the Skin the automatic skin would bind
; bone `i` to mesh bone `i` and bend the ribbon along the wrong bones, so no other golden, which
; binds through the automatic skin, shows a regression in the Skin binding.

